WEBVTT

00:00:00.280 --> 00:00:02.036
Give each phase point a mass.

00:00:02.036 --> 00:00:04.762
Their balance point gives the height of the graph.

00:00:05.092 --> 00:00:07.018
Degree two has three phases.

00:00:07.018 --> 00:00:10.830
Their angles are twice t, zero, and minus twice t.

00:00:11.160 --> 00:00:12.640
The weights add to one.

00:00:12.640 --> 00:00:17.007
Three eighths, one quarter, and three eighths are all positive.

00:00:17.337 --> 00:00:19.024
Set t to sixty degrees.

00:00:19.024 --> 00:00:21.415
The three phase points form a triangle.

00:00:21.415 --> 00:00:23.634
Their weighted mean is its balance point.

00:00:23.964 --> 00:00:26.206
The two mirror points have equal mass.

00:00:26.206 --> 00:00:30.814
Their imaginary parts cancel, so the balance point sits on the real axis.

00:00:31.144 --> 00:00:32.590
Read the balance point.

00:00:32.590 --> 00:00:36.692
At x equal to one half, P two takes the value minus one eighth.

